      "math_academy_id": "e-13383",
      "problem": "What is $-2.5 - 4.5?$",
      "worked_solution": "To subtract $4.5$ from $-2.5,$ we break up $4.5$ into its whole number part ($4$) and its decimal part ($0.5$) and proceed in two steps.\n\n- First, we subtract the whole number part. We start at $-2.5$ on the number line and move $4$ places to the left, which brings us to $-6.5.$\n\n- Then, we subtract the decimal part. We move the remaining $0.5$ places to the left, leaving us at $-7.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14149078/assets/53e5b15019c3189519b0fb4801e2ead2d9cd954d7da84640bb684215e53aca7a.png)\n\nThis gives $-2.5 - 4.5 = -7.0.$",
